2026-09-27T12:05:52.7057957Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7058307Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7058646Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7059558Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7060391Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7060491Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7060721Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7060998Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7061261Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7061346Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7127211Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7127546Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7127761Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7128142Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7128372Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7128486Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7128805Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7129030Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7129214Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7129839Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7130279Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7130910Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7131405Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7131526Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7131960Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7132532Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7132812Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7133098Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7133536Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7133635Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7133838Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7133963Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7135299Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7136864Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7137140Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7137695Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7138756Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7139620Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7140266Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7140768Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7141275Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7141399Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7141673Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7141843Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7143102Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7144459Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7145177Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7146147Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:52.7146374Z 
